"""Enhanced Mock K0 Data - Rich Lifestyle Database

Multiple realistic scenarios with actual correlations:

1. MILK INTOLERANCE: Milk → stomach discomfort/bloating within 2h (4/6 times)
2. COFFEE & SLEEP: Evening coffee (after 4pm) → poor sleep quality (5/6 times)
3. LATE EATING & GERD: Eating after 8pm → acid reflux symptoms (6/8 times)
4. EXERCISE & MOOD: Morning workouts → better mood scores (7/8 times)
5. SCREEN TIME & SLEEP: >2h screens before bed → poor sleep (8/10 times)
6. SUGAR & ENERGY: High sugar → crash 2h later (6/7 times)
7. DEHYDRATION & HEADACHES: <4 cups water → headaches (5/6 times)
8. STRESS & ANXIETY: Work deadlines → elevated anxiety (7/9 times)

This enables intelligent responses across nutrition, fitness, sleep, and mental health topics.
"""

from datetime import datetime, timedelta

TEST_USER_ID = "user_12345"
BASE_TIME = datetime.now() - timedelta(days=90)


def _ts(days_offset: int, hours: int = 0, minutes: int = 0) -> str:
    """Generate ISO timestamp relative to BASE_TIME."""
    dt = BASE_TIME + timedelta(days=days_offset, hours=hours, minutes=minutes)
    return dt.isoformat()


